From: ZyPulse <121911521+ZyPulse-zy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH RFC] netlink: use typeof concat expression count when decoding keys

A typeof key retains its full expression list, while the legacy packed
32-bit datatype identifier retains at most six subtype slots. Decoding
from dtype->subtypes alone can therefore drop fields from an eleven-field
key. When the full key expression is available, use its expression count.

This candidate is verified by an internal-source component regression
linked to the built libnftables helpers. The isolated kernel list/text/JSON
round trip remains untested on this WSL1 host. Do not equate it with the
historical vendor mergesort assertion or submit as a confirmed crash fix.
---
--- a/src/netlink.c
+++ b/src/netlink.c
@@ -1457,8 +1457,10 @@
 	struct expr *concat, *expr, *n = NULL;
 	int off = dtype->subtypes;
 
-	if (set->key->etype == EXPR_CONCAT)
+	if (set->key->etype == EXPR_CONCAT) {
+		off = expr_concat(set->key)->size;
 		n = list_first_entry(&expr_concat(set->key)->expressions, struct expr, list);
+	}
 
 	concat = concat_expr_alloc(&data->location);
 	while (off > 0) {
